  answerBlock("A one-time Botox client comes in, gets their treatment, maybe leaves a review if you ask nicely, and then you hope they come back in four months. There's no guarantee. You're essentially starting over every single time. A lifetime client is someone inside a membership: someone who has a standing monthly investment with the practice. They're pre-committed. Their next appointment isn't a maybe. The revenue is predictable, the relationship is deeper, and their average annual spend is significantly higher. Most med spas never make that shift because the owner doesn't realize a membership is a retention tool, not just a loyalty perk. When it's designed correctly with the right pricing, the right inclusions, and the right 90-day onboarding experience, it completely changes the financial stability of the practice."),
