  questionBlock("🟡", 9, "You mentioned that 73% of membership cancellations happen in the first 90 days. What are med spas doing, or not doing, in those first three months that causes people to walk away?"),
  sp(160),

  questionBlock("🟢", 10, "What's the psychology behind why a client who pays $399 a month is more valuable to a practice than a client who comes in and spends $600 every few months?"),
  sp(80),
  answerBlock("It comes down to predictability and behavior. The $600 client is a transaction. You don't know when they're coming back, you can't plan around them, and they've got no ongoing commitment to the relationship. The $399 monthly member is invested. Their annual value is $4,788 before a single add-on, and because they're engaged and coming in regularly, they're far more likely to say yes to additional treatments. They also refer more because they're proud of their results and they've got an ongoing relationship with your team. But here's the piece most owners miss: the member is also far less price sensitive because they've already made the mental shift from 'is this worth it' to 'how do I get the most out of my membership.' That mindset change is worth more than the dollar difference."),
