  questionBlock("🟢", 15, "You have data showing that one negative review costs a med spa approximately 30 potential clients. Most owners don't take their review strategy seriously, why is that such an expensive mistake?"),
  sp(80),
  answerBlock("Because reviews are the first thing a new client checks before they ever call you, and aesthetics is one of the highest-trust purchase decisions someone makes. People are putting their face in your hands. They're going to read every review. A negative review without a response, or a thin review profile overall, creates doubt. And in this industry, doubt means they close the tab and call someone else. The mistake most owners make is treating reviews as a nice-to-have instead of a revenue driver. When you look at the data on how many potential clients are researching you online before they ever contact you, and how dramatically a strong review profile increases conversion, it becomes very clear that your reputation isn't a marketing asset, it's a sales asset."),
