  sp(160),

  questionBlock("🟢", 28, "What's the difference between marketing that makes a practice look good and marketing that actually makes the phone ring and the calendar fill?"),
  sp(80),
  answerBlock("Marketing that makes you look good is built around the brand. Beautiful photos, aesthetic feeds, on-trend content. And those things matter, but they're not the same as marketing that converts. Marketing that makes the phone ring is built around the client: what they're worried about, what they want to feel, what's stopping them from booking, and what would make them trust you enough to come in. The shift we make with our clients is from broadcasting features to creating emotional connection. Stop writing about what you offer and start writing about how your client wants to feel. When your content speaks directly to someone's desire or frustration, it creates response. It creates DMs, inquiries, and booked appointments. Pretty content gets saved. Resonant content gets acted on."),
