  answerBlock("Because revenue isn't a marketing problem. It's a systems problem. An agency can drive a hundred leads a month and if the front desk isn't trained to convert, if there's no follow-up sequence, if there's no membership offer, if the pricing structure doesn't support upsells, those leads evaporate. You've paid for an audience and then failed to build a business with them. When we come in, we're looking at the full revenue cycle: how clients find you, how they're converted, what they're offered, how they're retained, and what they tell their friends. That's not something a single-function vendor can solve. It requires someone willing to get into the operations and install the infrastructure. That's what makes our work different and why the results stick."),
